WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.928 --> 00:00:16.548
watched as Miles paced the room in frustration.

2
00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:20.889
Several times Miles stopped and banged his fist on the table.

3
00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:24.870
"I really don't understand," Edward said.

4
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.011
"It's very strange."

5
00:00:27.031 --> 00:00:30.332
"There's nothing strange about it at all."

6
00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:36.121
Miles hit the table again and shouted, "Hugh has been evil since he was a child!"

7
00:00:38.503 --> 00:00:41.685
"No, I was talking about myself," Edward said.

8
00:00:41.705 --> 00:00:45.849
"The countryside should be filled with people looking for me.

9
00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.573
I don't understand why no one has noticed that the king is missing."

10
00:00:53.055 --> 00:00:56.357
Once again Edward wondered if Tom was pretending to be the king.

11
00:00:57.378 --> 00:00:59.200
Was that why no one was searching for him?

12
00:01:01.508 --> 00:01:03.529
"I'm sorry," Miles said.

13
00:01:03.549 --> 00:01:07.770
"I was so busy with my own troubles that I forgot about yours."

14
00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.691
"Well, I have an idea.

15
00:01:15.612 --> 00:01:23.234
I'll write a letter in three languages—Latin, Greek, and English—and you'll take it to my chief adviser.

16
00:01:24.855 --> 00:01:29.116
After Lord Hertford reads the letter, he'll send for me right away."

17
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.724
"It might be better to wait until I've sorted things out here," Miles said.

18
00:01:34.744 --> 00:01:41.830
"Then I'll be in a better position to—" Now it was Edward's turn to bang his fist on

19
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:42.770
the table and shout.

20
00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:47.334
"Your concerns are trivial compared to the fate of my kingdom!"

21
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:53.479
Then Edward spoke in a gentle voice, as if to apologize.

22
00:01:53.499 --> 00:01:55.021
"Don't worry.

23
00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.684
After I'm crowned, I'll make things right for you."

24
00:02:01.832 --> 00:02:05.654
While Edward sat at the table and wrote his letter, Miles thought about Edith.

25
00:02:05.674 --> 00:02:10.397
"She must have recognized me," he thought.

26
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:14.759
"But she said that she didn't, and Edith would never lie."

27
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.661
Edward finished his letter and handed it to Miles.

28
00:02:18.681 --> 00:02:22.783
"Take this straight to the palace first thing tomorrow."

29
00:02:24.364 --> 00:02:28.066
Distracted by his own problems, Miles stuck the letter in his pocket.

30
00:02:29.787 --> 00:02:32.933
Just then the door opened, and Edith entered the room.

31
00:02:33.954 --> 00:02:38.398
Her face was still pale and sad, but she held her head up as she approached Miles.

32
00:02:39.619 --> 00:02:41.681
He stepped forward eagerly to meet her.

33
00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:44.643
"Edith, my darling!

34
00:02:45.644 --> 00:02:53.310
I knew you recognized me, and now you've come back—" "Please stop talking and sit down," Edith said

35
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:54.191
as she took a seat.

36
00:02:54.211 --> 00:02:56.092
"I have only a few minutes.

37
00:02:57.914 --> 00:03:00.136
My husband is gathering some men to arrest you.

38
00:03:00.984 --> 00:03:01.784
They'll be here soon."

39
00:03:03.765 --> 00:03:10.448
Miles winced at the words "my husband," but he pulled a chair closer to hers.

40
00:03:11.048 --> 00:03:13.629
Edward, who was still standing, cleared his throat.

41
00:03:13.649 --> 00:03:15.730
"Oh, Your Majesty!"

42
00:03:16.351 --> 00:03:17.791
Miles sprang from his seat.

43
00:03:17.811 --> 00:03:20.512
"I should have let you sit down first."

44
00:03:23.173 --> 00:03:25.554
Miles quickly moved another chair next to his own.

45
00:03:26.435 --> 00:03:28.896
Then he remained standing until Edward was seated.

46
00:03:30.256 --> 00:03:33.839
Edith watched the whole scene with a puzzled look but didn't comment.

47
00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:40.924
Finally, when Miles was seated once again and gazing devotedly at her, she began to speak.

48
00:03:40.944 --> 00:03:44.186
"I've come to warn you that you must leave at once.

49
00:03:45.387 --> 00:03:49.410
Not only did you attack my husband, but you are a threat to everything he has.

50
00:03:50.871 --> 00:03:54.073
It's especially dangerous for you because you look so much like our Miles."

51
00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:58.156
"But I am Miles!"

52
00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.661
"I know you think you're Miles."

53
00:04:02.181 --> 00:04:03.001
Edith paused.

54
00:04:03.021 --> 00:04:08.404
"And by the respectful way you address your friend, you also think he's the king."

55
00:04:08.424 --> 00:04:12.186
"But I am the king!"

56
00:04:12.806 --> 00:04:13.546
Edward cried.

57
00:04:14.647 --> 00:04:15.927
Edith ignored Edward.

58
00:04:15.947 --> 00:04:22.731
"If you didn't look so much like Miles," she went on, "my husband might leave you alone.

59
00:04:23.891 --> 00:04:25.672
But now he'll deny that you're his brother.

60
00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.843
No one will dare to challenge him because he holds power over everyone who lives nearby."

61
00:04:30.863 --> 00:04:34.226
"Of course that's what the scoundrel will do."

62
00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.968
Miles knelt before Edith and took her hand.

63
00:04:37.988 --> 00:04:43.132
"And if you deny knowing me, then everyone who is dependent on Hugh will do the same.

64
00:04:44.233 --> 00:04:50.157
But if you say you know me Edith blushed and pulled her hand away.

65
00:04:50.177 --> 00:04:53.440
"Apparently you still don't understand the danger.

66
00:04:54.428 --> 00:04:56.650
My husband is a tyrant who shows no pity.

67
00:04:57.771 --> 00:04:58.752
He'll destroy you!"

68
00:05:03.175 --> 00:05:04.496
Edward burst out laughing.

69
00:05:04.516 --> 00:05:08.520
"Obviously you haven't seen Sir Miles in action.

70
00:05:09.741 --> 00:05:12.143
He's the bravest knight in my kingdom!

71
00:05:13.163 --> 00:05:15.045
Hugh is the one who should be afraid."

72
00:05:15.065 --> 00:05:19.929
"Thank you for those kind words, Your Majesty," Miles said.

73
00:05:19.949 --> 00:05:24.213
"If it's lack of money that's keeping you here, take this."

74
00:05:25.514 --> 00:05:27.175
Edith held out a purse to Miles.

75
00:05:27.195 --> 00:05:30.357
"Escape while you can, poor man.

76
00:05:31.478 --> 00:05:32.759
It's a matter of life and death!"

77
00:05:34.341 --> 00:05:36.442
Miles waved away the purse as he stood up.

78
00:05:36.462 --> 00:05:39.485
"I want only one thing.

79
00:05:40.546 --> 00:05:46.250
Look me in the eye, Edith, and answer this question: Am I Miles Hendon?"

80
00:05:48.912 --> 00:05:50.373
Edith looked steadily at him.

81
00:05:50.393 --> 00:05:54.770
"No, I don't know you," she said quietly.

82
00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.373
"I can't believe this!"

83
00:05:57.934 --> 00:05:58.695
Miles said.

84
00:06:00.076 --> 00:06:03.401
Before she could reply, several men burst into the room.

85
00:06:05.944 --> 00:06:08.467
They dragged Miles and Edward off to jail.
